From 824e0ae4f2433554a974a425d7397a75ad4989ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: medium <medium@debian.debian>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:53:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Proxy: Pass a TCP half-close on between the client and
 freedom

A target that closed after its answer reached the client only once the
inbound's uplinkOnly timer (1 s by default) ran out on the idle upload,
and a client's FIN never reached the target, so a target that answers on
EOF never answered. Freedom now ends what it sends to the target when
the client is done, and SOCKS, HTTP CONNECT and dokodemo-door end what
they send to the client when the answer is done. Only plain TCP and Unix
sockets are half-closed: TLS and transports are left as they were.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
